      "content": "You are correct that instilling pride and social cohesion are legitimate and vital goals for any school board, but they are not mutually exclusive with teaching about systemic injustices. A truly effective curriculum doesn't choose between \"triumphs\" and \"struggles\" but rather shows how our shared values were forged through the very conflicts and power dynamics you mentioned. Ignoring the heavy stuff to build a simple foundation of pride ultimately creates a fragile patriotism that fails to prepare students for the real complexities of the world they will inherit.",
